WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.719
DC Extended Universe fans, rejoice.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:09.500
Warner Bros. just dropped a new poster promoting
the forthcoming Wonder Woman 1984 film, and

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.840
the visual content is rather revealing.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:17.720
Wonder Woman 1984 is the follow-up to 2017's
Wonder Woman, one of the better-received entries

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:22.740
in Warner Bros.' mostly troubled attempt to
contend with the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:27.179
Considering the popularity of the original
film and its leading lady, fans have been

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:31.220
eager to devour this sequel since it was announced
back in 2018.

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:36.260
Sadly, Wonder Woman 1984 has had a pretty
tortured path to the big screen since that

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:37.360
announcement.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:43.620
Warner Bros. originally slated Wonder Woman
1984 for a December 2019 release, then pushed

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:47.560
that date up to November 2019, then to June
2020.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:51.080
It just wasn't fair to fans, and then it got
even worse.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.260
"You expect the battle to be fair!

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.040
A battle will never be fair!"

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:05.760
Wonder Woman 1984 was recently delayed again,
though by only a few months.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:10.780
The film is still slated for a summer release,
August 14, 2020, to be precise.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:15.160
Warner Bros. must be pretty committed to this
ambitious new date, because the studio has

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:19.820
already started pulling out the big promotional
guns, releasing a new poster that reveals

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:21.540
some important information.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:26.320
If we're being honest with ourselves, any
new poster featuring Gal Gadot as Wonder Woman

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:30.580
seems like a newsworthy development, but this
one has elevated significance.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:36.360
The latest art from the film is a kaleidoscopic
blast of color centered on Gadot in her Golden

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:37.400
Eagle armor.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:42.700
The battle suit first debuted in the third
issue of Elseworlds: Kingdom Come, a short

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:47.470
Wonder Woman and Superman crossover comic
story from creators Alex Ross and Mark Waid

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:49.760
that DC ran in 1996.

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:55.100
Unlike Wonder Woman 1984, Kingdom Come takes
place in the near future and concerns the

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:59.750
original Justice League's efforts to thwart
a new generation of meta-humans that pursue

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:02.340
the superhero trade through violent means.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:07.040
It's in the middle of this conflict that Wonder
Woman busts out her new golden threads.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:11.680
Since Kingdom Come, many other Wonder Woman
stories have featured the Golden Eagle armor,

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.980
including Wonder Woman #144, Our Worlds at
War, and Rise of an Olympian.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:21.720
Will we see some elements from these popular
comic arcs adapted into the feature film?

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.220
Only time will tell.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:28.540
Given the film's 1984 setting, its plot likely
won't address any of the cliffhangers set

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:33.260
up by 2017's Justice League, but it still
promises to be an entertaining romp full of

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:34.880
action, humor, and heart.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.140
"Have you ever been in love?"

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.340
"A long, long time ago."

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:39.240
"You?"

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.500
"So many times, yeah.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.400
All the time."

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:45.420
Aside from the new look, the most important
piece of information on the poster is the

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:50.680
confirmation that Warner Bros. plans to forge
ahead with Wonder Woman 1984's late summer

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:51.640
release date.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:56.600
This is quite the scheduling flex, since the
sequel flick could be pushed back yet again,

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:59.380
depending on when it's safe to return to movie
theaters.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:04.680
It would be pretty hard to imagine Warner
Bros. letting such an important, and expensive,

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:09.440
film play to empty seats; for now, we can
at least appreciate the studio's optimism.

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:14.320
Fans who have already been burned twice before
by thwarted release dates for Wonder Woman

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:18.300
1984 await the new August drop with cautious
optimism.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:22.880
Many other big films have been delayed this
year, including the latest James Bond flick,

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:26.020
the live-action Mulan movie, and The New Mutants.

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:30.491
None of those projects have dared to cement
a summer theatrical release in writing, let

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:33.040
alone in expensive marketing materials.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:38.800
Alongside Gadot's Diana Prince, Warner Bros.
has already confirmed that Wonder Woman 1984

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:43.150
will feature the return of Chris Pine's Steve
Trevor, though just how that will be possible

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:47.500
within the DCEU's internal logic has been
a topic of heated debate.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:52.400
As you'll remember, Steve seemingly died at
the end of the first Wonder Woman movie.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:57.780
Also confirmed is Kristen Wiig, who will portray
the villainous Cheetah, and Pedro Pascal as

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:59.160
Maxwell Lord.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:04.640
Although neither Wiig nor Pascal is featured
in the latest poster for Wonder Woman 1984,

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:08.200
fans are equally eager to see how they bring
their characters to the screen.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:11.060
With any luck, we'll find out by August 14th.

